---
source: system/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"lsipc\")"
---
List information on IPC facilities.

Modern replacement for ipcs. Reads /proc/sysvipc/* and /proc/sys/kernel/* to display IPC resource
information in tabular format.

Usage: lsipc [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -m, --shmems
          List shared memory segments

  -q, --queues
          List message queues

  -s, --semaphores
          List semaphore arrays

  -g, --global
          Show system-wide usage and limits

      --noheadings
          Suppress table headers

  -b, --bytes
          Show sizes in bytes

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
